/* book Worked example: Q: 1 kg of air (ideal gas, R = 0.287 kJ/(kg·K)) is compressed slowly and isothermally at 300 K from 100 kPa to 500 kPa. Find ΔU, ΔH, ΔS, ΔA and ΔG, and the least work needed.
   1. Ideal gas at constant T: ΔU = 0 and ΔH = 0, because u and h depend on T only.
   2. Entropy: ΔS = −mR·ln(p₂/p₁) = −1 × 0.287 × ln 5 = −0.287 × 1.6094 = −0.4619 kJ/K.
   3. Helmholtz: ΔA = ΔU − TΔS = 0 − 300 × (−0.4619) = +138.6 kJ.
   4. Gibbs: ΔG = ΔH − TΔS = 0 + 138.6 = +138.6 kJ, equal to ΔA because Δ(pV) = mRΔT = 0.
   5. Work: at constant T, W ≤ −ΔA = −138.6 kJ, so at least 138.6 kJ must be done on the gas. Check: reversible isothermal work = mRT·ln(p₂/p₁) = 0.287 × 300 × 1.6094 = 138.6 kJ.
   Answer: ΔU = ΔH = 0; ΔS = −0.4619 kJ/K; ΔA = ΔG = +138.6 kJ; the least work input is 138.6 kJ. */
